      "text": "To determine the smallest number of gold coins that satisfies the conditions of the problem, we can set up a series of congruences based on the given remainders when the number of coins is divided by 6 and 5. Let \\( N \\) be the number of coins.\n\nThe first condition tells us that when \\( N \\) is divided by 6, the remainder is 4. This can be written as:\n\\[ N \\equiv 4 \\pmod{6} \\]\nThis means that \\( N = 6k + 4 \\) for some integer \\( k \\).\n\nThe second condition tells us that when \\( N \\) is divided by 5, the remainder is 3. This can be written as:\n\\[ N \\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\]\nWe can substitute \\( N = 6k + 4 \\) into the second congruence:\n\\[ 6k + 4 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSimplifying this, we get:\n\\[ 6k + 4 \\equiv k + 4 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSubtracting 4 from both sides, we have:\n\\[ k \\equiv -1 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSince \\(-1 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5}\\), we can write:\n\\[ k \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5} \\]\nThis means that \\( k = 5m + 4 \\) for some integer \\( m \\). Substituting \\( k = 5m + 4 \\) back into the expression for \\( N \\), we get:\n\\[ N = 6(5m + 4) + 4 = 30m + 24 + 4 = 30m + 28 \\]\nTherefore, the smallest number of coins that satisfies both conditions is when \\( m = 0 \\):\n\\[ N = 28 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by 7:\n\\[ 28 \\div 7 = 4 \\text{ with a remainder of } 0 \\]\nSo, the number of coins left when equally divided among seven people is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).\n\nThe origins of the Universe lie over 14 billion years ago, and the Milky Way was formed about 10 billion years ago, which is 2 billion years later than the Sun. Therefore, the Sun had been formed when the Milky Way was still in the process of formation, which means we can form the Milky Way with composed materials from other materials of the universe. Which of the following statements about comets and other celestial materials in the universe is incorrect? \nSince the 21st century, humans have launched a large number of satellites, including man-made satellites, deep space probes, and laboratory robots. The construction of deep space probes and space laboratories is mainly based on materials laying an important foundation in the 21st century. To enhance the ability of dynamic imaging and remote sensing, the construction of high-grade laboratory robots was planned. The Mars rover, Tianwen 1, consists of a vehicle body and a mobile platform, the Mars probe is only a simple part. Made of large-power batteries, its heat dissipation and cooling functions can not only maintain the flexibility of its own surroundings and protect the ground rover but also ensure the integrity of the whole body. According to this information, which of the following statements is correct? \nA. The \"Mars rover\" is composed of metal materials. \nB. Comets mainly consist of metal materials. \nC. Laboratory robots are composed of carbon materials. \nD. Deep-space probes are mainly composed of diamond crystals. \nAnswer:\n0,3\n\nA piece of wood is 6m long, it is cut into 3 equal parts. Cut off 2 pieces each time, the parts are cut off in___\nA. Unequal\nB. Equal\nC. Unable to determine\nAnswer:\nA\n\nThe following is the evolution of international rankings for the world's stronger developed countries in three areas - per capita GDP, population, and youth and middle age population. The causes of changes in these three indicators of population growth are ____ | Data > Country Area | Country Area | | --- | --- | | Europe | Japan | Germany | United Kingdom | France | Central Africa | Canada | Australia and New Zealand | | 2000 | 1.53 million people per square kilometer | 1.44 million people per square kilometer | 2.02 million people per square kilometer | 0.78 million people per square kilometer | 982 people per square kilometer | 5.29 people/km^2 | 3.94 people/km^2 | 3.77 people/km^2 | 2.64 people/km^2 | | 2000-2013 | Integrated population of 397 million | | Germany: 35.50 | | 483 | | Canada: 31.27 | | 236 | | 841 | N/A | | 2000-2013 | 100 | |\nA. Changing from development to improvement\nB. The number of deaths in Europe, Japan, and Germany is large\nC. Increase in farmers, decline in industrial workers\nD. Decrease in birth rates in these countries and regions\nAnswer:\nD\n\nPlace a mixture of sodium chlorate and potassium chlorate in an evaporating dish and heat it until the solid gradually decreases. What is the remaining solid?\nA. Potassium chlorate\nB. Sodium chloride and potassium chlorate\nC. Sodium chloride and potassium hydroxide\nD. Sodium chlorate, potassium chlorate, and water\nAnswer:\nD\n\nWhich of the following chemical equations does NOT result in a solution with a pH < 7?\nA. A small amount of clear lime water is added to an acidic solution.\nB. An appropriate amount of dilute hydrochloric acid is added to sodium hydroxide solution.\nC. A small amount of slaked lime is added to acidic solutions of sodium carbonate substances.\nD. A small amount of sodium carbonate reacts with dilute hydrochloric acid.\nAnswer:\nC\n\nThe main reason why Jerusalem becomes a holy city for Jews, Christians, and Muslims worldwide is because this city ___.\nA. has a beautiful environment\nB. is located on a plain\nC. has good farming conditions\nD. contains significant religious symbols\nAnswer:\nD",
